returned_finding_id	P1-raw-execution-still-reachable-through-v7
returned_finding	v8 imports runV7 from track-b2c-000197-v11-v6-direct-pg-regression-v7.mjs, where runV7 remains exported and takes a caller-supplied authority.target without calling intakeV7 or intakeV8. The v8 module's public API is sealed, but the raw Docker/psql execution function remains directly importable from the retained v7 module and is the function v8 delegates to.
impact	The returned v7 execution-bypass condition is not eliminated repository-wide: a Docker-capable caller can invoke the old exported runV7 path and avoid every v8 gate.
required_correction	Move raw execution into a non-exported private module/function that is not independently importable, or make runV7 itself enforce the v8 sealed authority. Add an import-level regression that attempts the former raw path without all immutable inputs and proves zero child/Docker calls.

returned_finding_id_2	P2-identity-registry-incomplete
returned_finding_2	The immutable registry lists G/H and the prior isolated v4 run/container/database, but omits C/D and E/F run/container/database identities and omits all C/D/E/F anonymous volume IDs; even the isolated v4 volume is absent. The resource check can therefore accept a v8 authority reusing an omitted prior anonymous volume, while the registry's prohibited_classes field is not machine-enforced.
impact_2	The registry proves only absence from a partial inventory, not absence from all A-F, G/H, and previous fault-regression resources as required.
required_correction_2	Replace the partial registry with a frozen complete inventory of every historical A-H and fault-regression runId, container full ID/name, database, and anonymous volume ID, and machine-check all four target fields against it before evidence or Docker access. Bind that full inventory SHA through candidate, reviews, and resource authority.
status_after_review	NO-GO-for-resource-create-or-execute-until-P1-and-P2-corrected-and-fresh-DB-QA-DRAIN-RESOURCE-GOs
